## SUBJECT
Every site that READS or WRITES `isRule`, classified by whether it can see a node
whose groupBody is SHARED -- i.e. a copy made by GroupItem::GroupItem(GroupItem*),
which does `groupBody = grup->groupBody` while rStuff stays per-node and null.

## WHY IT IS BEING MEASURED
literalMasterIsRule option B = stop the back-propagation (raise isRule somewhere
per-node, or gate the write). Its blast radius is the ONLY unknown standing
between B and the cheaper options A and C. This census measures that radius.

## SCOPE
HAND-WRITTEN SOURCE ONLY: *.twk, *.rtn (the *.mm are GENERATED from these and
counting both double-counts), plus the incant corpus (incant/, minionWork/,
genLadder/).
SPELLINGS: tok/C++ source uses bare `isRule`; incant uses `isRulE`.
⚠ H9: prose and comments must be separated from code. A file COUNT is not a site
count, and the classification -- not the grep -- is the finding.

## CONTROLS -- ALL THREE MUST APPEAR IN THE RAW HITS OR THE CENSUS IS VOID
C1  WRITE  GroupItem.twk setRuleStuff -- the back-propagating write itself.
           [CONFIRMED PRESENT at :1879-1880 before registration was closed]
C2  READ   auditMissingRules -- reads isRule && !rStuff; it is the instrument
           that SURFACED this whole problem. A census excluding it is void.
C3  READ   the incant population walks (odoPopulation / countPopulation), which
           filter on `if !isRulE;` and are how the six masters entered the
           genParse population.

## DECISION RULE -- fixed BEFORE the numbers, so the answer cannot be fitted after
Under B the flag is raised on STRICTLY FEWER nodes. So a read changes its answer
only where it currently sees a back-propagated true. Classify every READ site:
  (a) WANTS-CORRECTED  -- a census/audit/population read that is currently WRONG
                          because of back-propagation. B fixes it.
  (b) INDIFFERENT      -- cannot receive a shared-body copy, or does not care.
  (c) LOAD-BEARING     -- relies on the back-propagated true being there today;
                          B would change live behaviour here.

  B IS SAFE  iff (c) is EMPTY.
  B IS COSTED, NOT REFUSED, if (c) is non-empty: each (c) site is named with
             what it would need instead.
  ⚠ A LARGE (a) COUNT IS NOT EVIDENCE AGAINST B -- it is evidence FOR it, and
    that asymmetry is registered now so a big number is not misread later as
    a big radius.

## PREDICTION, with its mechanism, per H11's "predict mechanisms not counts"
The WRITE is one site (setRuleStuff), because that is the only place the flag is
raised from a registry/parent test. MECHANISM: modify() and every attach path
funnel through it.
At least one (c) is EXPECTED, mechanism: parse-time dispatch tests isRule to
decide whether a node is a rule at all, and terms attached to rules are exactly
the shared-body copies. If (c) comes back EMPTY, that is a surprise and gets
re-checked before it is reported.

