## FINDING 3 -- tokenize IS NOT THIS DISEASE. Clay's premise needs one correction.
The relayed suspicion was that tokenize, break, continue and return "all carry
isRule only through the same back-propagation". Measured against the audit:

    tokenize                 ABSENT from MISSRULE  => it HAS rStuff
    break/continue/return    PRESENT in MISSRULE   => isRule, no rStuff

tokenize gets `modify(strap,"^@")` called DIRECTLY on the master, not on a copy,
so it legitimately owns both flag and rStuff. It is excluded from countPop's 39
by the has-a-list filter and appears in the odometer's 64 only because that
filter does not test for a list. So the tokenize question is REAL but it is a
POPULATION question, not a shared-body question, and it is not blocked on this.
⚠ break/continue/return ARE in the affected population, but by a different route
-- they are Keywords members reached by ruleActions.rtn:449's bin propagation,
not by a groupBody share. THREE mechanisms, not one.

